---
layout: changelog
title: Preview deployments now require authentication
date: 2026-09-17
cover: /images/blog/authenticated-site-previews/cover.avif
tags: sites, security
---

Preview deployments created by automatic Git deployments now require an Appwrite account that belongs to the site's organization. Pushing a branch still builds a preview and posts its link, but the link only opens for people you have invited to the organization, so a preview URL no longer works for anyone who finds it.

The first time you open a preview, Appwrite asks you to authorize **Appwrite Preview** with the account you are signed in with. Authorizing grants the single **View your identity** permission, which confirms who you are so Appwrite can check your organization membership. Nothing needs to be configured on your site or project.

